---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { evidenceCopy } from '../../data/site';
---
<SiteLayout
  locale="en"
  title="About"
  description="About OPC Vibe Stack, how updates work, evidence labels, and the disclaimer."
  canonicalPath="/en/about/"
>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    OPC Vibe Stack is an English-first knowledge site for one-person companies using
    Claude Code, Codex, and Grok Build across research, build, and sell.
  </p>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What this is</h2>
    <p>
      Executable checklists and tool-division guidance—not a news dump, course platform, or
      unofficial vendor ranking. The site itself is dogfooded with the same agent stack.
    </p>

    <h2>How updates work</h2>
    <p>
      Daily Vibe Coding briefings (English X–first) feed a weekly editorial pass.
      Documentation-backed guidance and briefing-derived changes go through checks of original
      sources, tool versions, and evidence labels before publication.
    </p>

    <h2>Evidence labels</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Tested</strong> — {evidenceCopy.tested}</li>
      <li><strong>Documentation-backed</strong> — {evidenceCopy['documentation-backed']}</li>
      <li><strong>Unverified</strong> — {evidenceCopy.unverified}</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="disclaimer">Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      This site is <strong>unofficial</strong> and not affiliated with Anthropic, OpenAI, xAI, or
      other tool vendors. Security decisions are yours: do not paste secrets into agents, and verify
      extensions and SSH keys yourself. Numbers and third-party claims may be unverified even when
      a public source is linked. Follow evidence labels. Nothing here is legal, financial, or
      compliance advice—especially for hardware supply chain and certifications.
    </p>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
